    with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
        return sum(1 for _ in f)
```

Using `errors="replace"` (or `"ignore"`) prevents the program from crashing when it encounters malformed or unexpected bytes, though it may corrupt unusual characters during processing. This trade-off is acceptable if you only need to count lines rather than preserve the content accurately.

