The solution is to use an arrow function instead, since arrow functions don't have their own `this`—they capture `this` from the surrounding `start()` method:

```javascript
start() {
  setInterval(() => {
    this.seconds += 1;
    console.log(this.seconds);
  }, 1000);
}
```

